/athletes/132152"} "Abbey Weitzeil"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/132163"} "Simone Manuel"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Note that that list did not include Denmark’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/123149"} "Pernille Blume"] ", previously known primarily as a short-course sprinter. Despite the absence of any turns, she came through in Rio for the gold medal, setting a Danish record of 24.07, with Manuel taking silver in 24.09. The bronze was another upset, going to Belarussian " [:a {:href "/athletes/116762"} "Aleksandra Gerasimenya"] ", who had been the silver medalist in London, but done very little since then. Cate and Bronte finished fifth and seventh, respectively, in what was a very disappointing Olympics for them. The final was incredibly close, with only 12/100ths of a second separating 1st and 6th place."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123149"} "Pernille Blume"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/DEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/DEN.png"}] "DEN"]] [:td {} "24.23 (1 h12)"] [:td {} "24.28 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "24.07 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/132163"} "Simone Manuel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "24.71 (4 h11)"] [:td {} "24.44 (4 h2)"] [:td {} "24.09 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/116762"} "Aliaksandra Herasimenia"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BLR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2